            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "9df87bff-2933-4014-8de8-47b4a8145df8",
            "type": "sourceText",
            "position": {
                "x": -80,
                "y": 160
            },
            "size": {
                "width": 660,
                "height": 800
            },
            "config": {
                "text": "Word Fall is a turn-based casual word puzzle game that combines mechanics from classic Scrabble, popular Match-3 games, and Tetris.\nGame Concept: The player forms words using letter blocks arranged on a grid. Once a word is formed, the used letters disappear, the blocks above drop down due to gravity, and new letters fall in from the top.\n2. Key Gameplay Features\nFree Letter Selection Across the Board:\nUnlike most word games where letters must be connected via a continuous line, here the player can select suitable letters from any part of the game board.\nCompactness Bonus (Adjacency Bonus / Clusters):\nIt is advantageous for the player to select letters located next to each other (horizontally, vertically, or diagonally).\nThe more tightly grouped the letters of the formed word are on the board, the higher the score multiplier (e.g., 2 adjacent letters double the score, 3 triple it, etc.). This adds an element of spatial strategy to the game.\nFalling Dynamics and Gravity:\nAfter a correctly formed word disappears from the board, the remaining blocks drop down—much like in Tetris—altering the layout of the remaining letters.\nSmart \"Letter Bag\" System (Balanced Spawning):\nNew letters do not fall completely at random; instead, they come from a specially balanced set (a \"bag\") with a strictly maintained ratio of vowels to consonants. This ensures the player never faces a situation where only unusable letters appear on the board. Level Objectives and Obstacles:\nThe game is divided into levels featuring move limits and specific tasks (e.g., scoring a certain number of points, breaking ice or chain blocks, or clearing tiles beneath the letters).\n3. In-game Boosters (Support Tools)\nBoosters are available to enhance engagement and assist in challenging situations:\n🔨 Hammer: Destroys any single obstructing letter on the board without using a move.\n🔀 Shuffle: Rearranges the current set of letters on the board if the player cannot spot any suitable words.\n💡 Smart Hint: Analyzes the board and highlights the highest-scoring or most advantageous available word.\n🃏 Joker (Wildcard): Transforms a selected letter into a wildcard symbol (?) that can represent any letter.\n⬆️ Score Doubler: Increases the point value of a specific letter on the board.\nTask and Objective System (Level Tasks & Objectives)\nTo keep gameplay engaging and ensure the difficulty ramps up from level to level, the game features a flexible system of objectives. To complete a level, the player must meet a set of conditions within a limited number of moves:\nCollecting specific words or combinations (3 to 5 tasks per level):\nSpecific words: A level may require forming a strictly defined list of words (e.g., \"Fear,\" \"Cream,\" \"Cup,\" \"Lid,\" \"Jar\").\nWord length categories: If a specific word list isn't set, the level generates dynamic tasks based on complexity (e.g., \"Form three 4-letter words\" or \"Form one 4-letter word and one 5-letter word\").\nLevel Finale — Scoring Points:\nThe final, mandatory condition for any level is always reaching the target score (Score Goal). It is defined in the configuration for each level. This ensures that the player does not merely complete local objectives but also strives to form the most advantageous and longest words, maximizing bonuses.\nCollect specific bonuses. — Collect the specific number of bonuses listed in the section below.\nClear all obstacles from the board.",
                "sourceName": ""
            },
            "inputs": [],
            "outputs": [
                {
                    "id": "51abf62f-e345-4cd9-a523-ea808f4cdf33",
                    "name": "out",
                    "type": "text"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "id": "ea075eb7-a537-41ab-93a0-bdb2cde9a64d",
            "type": "sourceText",
